[{:db/id "q-36010/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "5c0f6b3e-77a4-5114-9a8a-e1f304a8ce44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1fecb6c3-e227-5b30-a1d2-5b8b2fdcc4b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "480e0767-db4a-5fd3-9260-40855d6eef7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "26837314-0271-5c4e-a74f-980999b80d50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "627dfaec-dd9e-555c-9a00-1edccd5d30af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9861c43d-6fd9-56b1-9cb4-217ce804b08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36010/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-36010/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-36010/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-36010/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-36010/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-36010/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36010" :question/id #uuid "a802d1bc-5bd8-512e-a33b-811eae18f7fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-36010" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36010/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36010"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36039"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\n- $x\\in [-4,0]$\n- $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,1)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer/id #uuid "2e8f9e8c-9047-5a6a-a566-7c628516655b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "25309cc9-0c6a-54d8-8dfb-0fc2b32a6981" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "21499e87-a101-51de-9889-40e1414131a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "26a3be6d-a0f3-5e45-a2ea-e5f2626892d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7425990f-cecb-5f41-99b8-18f12baefd75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "144991a2-b665-55e4-814e-32353a9eec94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36934/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer-field/choices ["q-36934/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" "q-36934/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-36934/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-36934/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-36934/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36934" :question/id #uuid "75b2a4c0-9fd0-5022-a065-c7880b09f9c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-36934" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36934/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36934"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7766579a-d19d-52c0-a069-ba07a3f86eed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bd3a0213-e6fb-54df-8107-ee0148cf080c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1e4e615b-b8bd-5d55-a45c-968620500c37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a0f0c6c9-a3f0-5632-adc2-4914b9bb05a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e0867068-bc55-5ee9-898b-5c341a66317c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b3cb55c-3394-58c9-8fc9-5e66544e30a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66729/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-66729/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-66729/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-66729/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-66729/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-66729/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66729" :question/id #uuid "d0455465-8a85-5aa8-911c-68ab12f14b4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-66729" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-66729/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cc2498d4-c5e6-594e-9bc2-7feb3530daa2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1882bd91-c950-586a-a609-ab5ec7e41b2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "46fa9d60-f6f5-5b63-86a4-2449214ab6cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0e5e97c8-b041-516c-96ca-9b38b7ff41f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f0f25d39-db78-5394-b4d0-bc5544af92d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "78364d24-42eb-5b28-87c1-77b4f2b27aa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108667/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-108667/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-108667/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-108667/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-108667/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-108667/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108667" :question/id #uuid "07ce3cd4-47b8-5b1e-860e-1b9099cab604" :question/math-academy-id "q-108667" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/811ead4928d2f245235736dce473d121261ea358ca4ff3a0cc8b01bb2e9f3b31.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,3)$\n- $x\\in [1,4]$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/32f1ad5bdec30951900a1c30c2996ea040e65880f859c43769faf374db06a2f0.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,3)$ and $x\\in [1,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/8ed451b24fa83de513f4a1b5c79d39f94add784c6b7265e765a3381e7b03363a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108667/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108667"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
